From fdeac1d29d9abaa63a48c0c0b1d31d791f9a4228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dispatch Sandbox <jax1313@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:35:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Measure branch coverage, and measure the launcher

The gate was line-only. A line counts as covered the moment it runs once, so
every `if` whose false path was never taken read as fully covered -- and in this
repository the false paths are where the refusals live: the transition that is
not allowed, the token that expired, the truck with no capacity profile, the
transport that is UNCONFIGURED. A gate that cannot see an untested refusal is
not measuring the thing this program is most careful about.

And the packages differed between the two places they were named. .coveragerc
listed cin_lite and dispatch; the workflow added portal on the command line;
neither included dispatch_launcher -- 3,943 lines, and the thing that actually
starts the product on Mike's machine. So CI enforced one gate and a contributor
running `pytest --cov` locally got another. The workflow now passes a bare
--cov and .coveragerc is the single definition.

    branch coverage, four packages:  91.39%   (floor 90%)

The number is lower than the 94.74% it replaces because it is measuring more,
in a stricter way, across more code. Windows-only branches in the launcher stay
excluded by individual `pragma: no cover` marks, so what is not measured is
visible line by line instead of by a package being absent from a list.
---
 .coveragerc              | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 10 +++++++---
 CLAUDE.md                | 13 +++++++++----
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.coveragerc b/.coveragerc
index c81a62c..03179c8 100644
--- a/.coveragerc
+++ b/.coveragerc
@@ -1,13 +1,39 @@
 [run]
+# Branch coverage, not just line coverage.
+#
+# The gate was line-only (`branch = False`), which counts a line as covered the
+# moment it runs once. Every `if` in this repository whose false path was never
+# taken read as fully covered -- and the false paths are where the refusals
+# live: the transition that is not allowed, the token that has expired, the
+# truck with no capacity profile, the transport that is UNCONFIGURED. A gate
+# that cannot see an untested refusal is not measuring the thing this program
+# is most careful about.
+branch = True
+
 source =
     cin_lite
     dispatch
-branch = False
+    portal
+    # dispatch_launcher was outside the gate entirely -- 3,943 lines, and the
+    # thing that actually starts the product on Mike's machine. It is in now.
+    # Its Windows-only branches are marked `pragma: no cover` individually
+    # rather than the whole package being exempt, so what is excluded is
+    # visible line by line instead of by omission.
+    dispatch_launcher
+
+omit =
+    */__pycache__/*
+    */tests/*
 
 [report]
 show_missing = True
+skip_covered = False
 fail_under = 90
 exclude_lines =
     pragma: no cover
     if __name__ == .__main__.:
     raise NotImplementedError
+    if TYPE_CHECKING:
+    class .*\bProtocol\):
+    @(abc\.)?abstractmethod
+    \.\.\.$
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 396ed1f..9d81266 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -38,12 +38,16 @@ jobs:
           pip install -r portal/requirements.txt
           pip install pytest pytest-cov
 
+      # The packages and the branch setting come from .coveragerc alone.
+      # Naming them here as well meant the gate CI enforced and the gate a
+      # contributor got from `pytest --cov` locally were two different gates:
+      # .coveragerc listed cin_lite and dispatch, this file added portal, and
+      # neither included dispatch_launcher -- 3,943 lines, and the thing that
+      # actually starts the product.
       - name: Run test suite with coverage
         run: |
           python -m pytest \
-            --cov=cin_lite \
-            --cov=dispatch \
-            --cov=portal \
+            --cov \
             --cov-config=.coveragerc \
             --cov-report=term-missing \
             --cov-report=xml \
diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index 869f08a..58ec632 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -278,16 +278,21 @@ Do not mark an item verified without actual runtime evidence. Current readiness:
 
 ---
 
-## 8. Current build status (2026-08-25)
+## 8. Current build status (2026-09-12)
 
 | | |
 |---|---|
 | Version | `0.1.0` |
-| Suite | **3,696 passed** · 0 failed / 0 skipped / 0 warnings |
-| Gated coverage | **94.74%** over `cin_lite` + `dispatch` + `portal` (floor 90%) |
-| Ungated | `dispatch_launcher/` at 87.75% — Windows-only branches; see `docs/readiness/OPERATIONAL_PROOF.md` §2.1 |
+| Suite | **4,171 passed** · 0 failed / 0 skipped / 0 warnings |
+| Gated coverage | **91.39%** with **branch coverage** over `cin_lite` + `dispatch` + `portal` + `dispatch_launcher` (floor 90%) |
+| Ungated | nothing. `dispatch_launcher/` is inside the gate; its Windows-only branches are marked `pragma: no cover` line by line rather than the package being exempt |
 | Laptop readiness | **UNVERIFIED** — see below |
 
+The coverage figure went *down* and the gate got stronger. It was line-only, so
+every `if` whose false path was never taken read as covered — and the false
+paths are where the refusals live. Branch coverage counts them, and
+`dispatch_launcher/` is no longer outside the measurement.
+
